---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { PHONE, PHONE_TEL } from '../../../lib/site.ts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Foundation issues in the White Mountains & Show Low area"
  description="Independent floor elevation surveys and second opinions for Show Low, Pinetop-Lakeside, Snowflake, and the White Mountains. Local soil patterns and why measurement before repair matters here."
>
  <div class="container">
    <h1 class="page-title">Foundation issues in the White Mountains & Show Low area</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Homes in Show Low, Pinetop-Lakeside, Snowflake, Taylor, Heber-Overgaard and the surrounding White Mountains see the same cracks, sticking doors, and uneven floors that appear across Arizona — but with fewer local options for independent measurement.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>What is common here</h2>
      <p>
        Northern Arizona has its own mix of soils, elevation changes, and seasonal moisture. Many houses show long-standing differential movement that has been stable for years. Others have more recent changes tied to drainage, irrigation, or plumbing. The visible distress looks the same either way. The decision about whether repair is needed does not.
      </p>
      <p>
        Repair companies from the Valley travel up for work. That is normal. It also means the first person measuring your floors often has a financial interest in finding a project.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Why an independent survey helps in this market</h2>
      <p>
        Geotech and independent measurement coverage is thinner in the White Mountains than in Phoenix or Tucson. When a large repair bid arrives, many homeowners have no local, neutral source for a second look at the numbers.
      </p>
      <p>
        An independent floor elevation survey gives you:
      </p>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>A current contour map of the living floors</li>
        <li>A plain-language read of settlement vs heave patterns</li>
        <li>A practical watch list if monitoring makes more sense than immediate repair</li>
        <li>Clear questions to take back to any contractor</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Before you list or during a transaction</h2>
      <p>
        Realtors in the White Mountains Association of Realtors see foundation concerns surface both before listing and during the inspection period. A measured, independent conversation can keep a deal from stalling under a scary bid that no one fully understands.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is not a formal real-estate inspection product. It is practical measurement and judgment when foundation questions appear.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How we work up here</h2>
      <p>
        We are based in the 928. Surveys in Show Low, Pinetop, and the surrounding communities are scheduled by phone. We can often batch visits when several homeowners are ready in the same window. You know the fee before we drive.
      </p>
      <div class="contact-box">
        <p><strong>Call or text</strong></p>
        <a class="phone-link" href={`tel:${PHONE_TEL}`}>{PHONE}</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
